# ENTRY — Are the five proposed Colab compute operations the right split

Investigation: book 00.00.10.work, page 0701.colab-compute-ops, pass 05.01.
Prepared by Codex Prime (request drafted by the 0510/05.02 executor as a declared fixture) on 2026-10-29 for fresh Colab, unassigned. Reviewer: Codex Prime.
Every source here is the exact Git blob at workshop commit c406b2a9a3d8d9cc1c67c2c79a8e336989cc0eb1.
This entry is a draft brief. It releases, seats and authorizes nothing.

## Role and mode
You are a Colab. Mode: open-design.
You may challenge the method and propose a better one. Your findings are yours; they do not change any page by themselves.

## Question
Do the five proposed operations divide deterministic compute work from intelligence work at the right places, and which operation boundary is most likely to make Prime repeat manual work or lose a finding?

## Why this matters
If the split is wrong, the module either automates a judgement it should only record, or leaves Prime re-typing context and custody facts on every Colab. Both failures were seen before the design was recovered.

## Context
0411.colab designs a Colab support module. Its section on compute proposes five operations: prepare, verify, intake, review and find. The first implementation (0510.colab-tools/05.02) builds prepare, verify and intake only. Review and find are not built. Prime will use the tool on real work before a fresh Colab probes it.

## Built state
prepare, verify and intake exist as lab code that wraps the accepted pack assembler, custody checker, return capture helper and inspector. review and find exist only as the design text in the target section.

## Known gaps
G01. No investigation member exists in 0700.band.colabs yet; this binding names a declared fixture page.
G02. The workflow adapter that attaches a package to an investigation pass is being built separately and is not part of this package.
G03. Section ids have no declared syntax in interface v1, so only exact headings can select a section.

